      "location": "Baton Rouge Community College, LA",
      "description": "The Dean of Students Office at Baton Rouge Community College is committed to upholding and managing the College’s Student Code of Conduct, serving as a student advocate, aiding students in crisis, and supporting students by directing services and programs that provide life-enriching experiences and enhance students' education. Why would you contact the Dean of Students Office? You have questions about campus policies or procedures You are concerned about the well-being of a student You want to report a concerning incident You don't know where to go and need guidance The Dean of Students Office at BRCC also serves as a vital hub for student resources designed to address both immediate and long-term needs. From ensuring that students have access to essential resources like food and professional attire through initiatives like The Store and The Closet, to providing guidance and support during personal and academic challenges, the Dean of Students Office is dedicated to empowering students to succeed. These resources are part of BRCC’s commitment to removing barriers and fostering an environment where every student can thrive both inside and outside the classroom. Whether you need assistance navigating the complexities of campus life, support during a crisis, or simply need a helping hand, the Dean of Students Office is here to ensure you have the tools and resources you need to achieve your academic and personal goals.",
